# Repo-root .dockerignore for the apps/api Docker build (Render build context).
# Render sends the whole repository as the Docker build context, so exclude
# everything the backend image does not need — this keeps the context small and
# prevents secrets / large dirs from being uploaded to the builder.

# Frontend (deployed separately on Vercel) — never needed by the API image.
apps/web

# Version control + tooling metadata.
.git
.workbuddy-ai

# Python caches / virtualenvs / build artifacts.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.venv
**/.pytest_cache
**/*.egg-info
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache

# Node caches (in case frontend creeps into the context).
**/node_modules
**/.next

# Secrets — never bake these into an image.
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/.env.*.local

# Misc.
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
*.md
